Most warlocks use Voidwalkers because **Torment** allows them to tank multiple mobs via **Suffering** (AoE taunt), enabling efficient **Drain Tanking**—the dominant leveling strategy where the warlock Life Taps freely while the pet holds aggro. The Succubus lacks reliable threat generation, forcing the warlock to manage aggro manually or kite, which is slower and riskier despite higher raw damage. [end of text]


